  "pli-tv-kd17:1.2.9": "Sp-ṭ 4.330: <i lang='pi' translate='no'>Ujuṁ kārāpetabbanti puñjaṁ kārāpetabbaṁ</i>, “To be made straight means to be made into heaps.” It seems from this that the original meaning may have been <i lang='pi' translate='no'>ujuṁ kārāpetabbaṁ</i> rather than <i lang='pi' translate='no'>puñjaṁ kārāpetabbaṁ</i>. I interpret “to make straight” as organizing the harvest into sheaves. ",
