  "pli-tv-kd17:3.1.12": "<i lang='pi' translate='no'>Kheḷāsaka</i>, literally, “an eater of spittle”. The spittle apparently refers to the material support, honor, and praise he had acquired in an inappropriate manner. Sp 4.336 says: <i lang='pi' translate='no'>Kheḷāsakassāti ettha micchājīvena uppannapaccayā ariyehi vantabbā kheḷasadisā, tathārūpe paccaye ayaṁ ajjhoharatīti katvā kheḷāsakoti bhagavatā vutto</i>, “<i lang='pi' translate='no'>Kheḷāsakassa</i> here means that those requisites he had acquired through wrong livelihood, which the noble ones would vomit up like spittle, such requisites he has swallowed down. <i lang='pi' translate='no'>Kheḷāsakassa</i> was said by the Buddha in this connection.” ",
