  "pli-tv-kd17:5.4.12": "<i lang='pi' translate='no'>Samaggānañca anuggaho</i>, literally, “and the helping of those who are united”. The commentary to the parallel verse at <a href='https://suttacentral.net/iti19/en/brahmali#3.2'>Iti 19:3.2</a> says: <i lang='pi' translate='no'>Samaggānañcanuggahoti samaggānaṁ sāmaggianumodanena anuggaṇhanaṁ sāmaggianurūpaṁ, yathā te sāmaggiṁ na vijahanti, tathā gahaṇaṁ ṭhapanaṁ anubalappadānanti attho</i>, “<i lang='pi' translate='no'>Samaggānañcanuggaho</i> means: one who rejoices in unity helps those who are united in accordance with what is suitable for unity; he takes hold of it, firms it up, and supports it, so that they do not abandon that unity.” ",
