  "pli-tv-kd17:5.5.19": "The next segment is only found in MS, and is missing in the PTS edition. It could be rendered as follows: “He has the view that what he says is legitimate and the view that the schism is legitimate.” This seems to be a mistake in MS, since the whole point of this is that the monk “misrepresents his view of what’s true, his belief of what’s true, his acceptance of what’s true, or his sentiment of what’s true”. This assessment is supported by the fact that the parallel passage at <a href='https://suttacentral.net/pli-tv-pvr19/en/brahmali#80.1'>Pvr 19:80.1</a> does not have this combination. See Sp 5.477, which gives the details on this passage, which is only contracted in the Canonical text. ",
